{"diagnosis": "Trace window shows only tohost FAIL 0xdead with cpu trap asserted at CYCLES=2009 and no per-cycle rdata values, so exact data mismatch is unclear from logs. Excerpt line 384 selects stale mem_rdata_q on mem_xfer instead of live mem_rdata, so mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle/mem_rdata_latched captures the previous word. Wrong fetch word causes mis-decode/trap and FAIL in the NOP fetch test.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -384,1 +384,1 @@
-	assign mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle = (mem_xfer || LATCHED_MEM_RDATA) ? mem_rdata_q : mem_rdata;
+	assign mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle = (mem_xfer || LATCHED_MEM_RDATA) ? mem_rdata : mem_rdata_q;
", "expected": "tohost: PASS with TRAP deasserted and fetch alignment OK (checksum != c2a7a4d6295484feeb9ec1ea9381732b8e39a7ccd1997c7d70f6454da2fb4659, CYCLES progress past 2009)"}

